      formula: "Net fiscal benefit = utility from public services - taxes paid",
      substitution: "Substitute the values: 30,000 - 22,000",
      calculation: "30,000 - 22,000 = 8,000 birr of net fiscal benefit.",
      answer: "The household gains 8,000 birr per year; fiscal equalization aims to reduce or eliminate differences in such net fiscal benefits across regions."
